WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.826
The paper ablates its bound.

00:00:01.906 --> 00:00:04.956
The finite-rank error is an irreducible floor,

00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:10.332
while residue terms shrink at a log-N-over-N rate
and vanish for large samples.

00:00:10.412 --> 00:00:15.913
Dropped, the simplified bounds fail only in the
small-sample regime, as predicted.

00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:22.310
A ridge sweep shows the new bound improves toward
the ridgeless limit while the prior worsens.
